  "notes": [
    "Overrides restore license material missing from exact published Cargo packages. GitHub commit IDs come from each package .cargo_vcs_info.json.",
    "objc2 upstream LICENSE.md states the applicable licenses but does not supply a package-specific copyright line or full MIT text. The original statement is preserved along with the MIT permission/warranty terms from OSI; no copyright holder or year has been invented. Retain package author metadata and existing source notices.",
    "For Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT packages in the objc2 family, these collected terms document use under the MIT option. The upstream statement about derivation from Apple SDKs is preserved without alteration.",
    "selectors 0.36.1 source headers and Cargo metadata state MPL-2.0; the license text is obtained from Mozilla. Exact MPL-covered crate sources should be provided separately.",
    "Native zvec material is pinned to node binding commit 96fe5e09619369179d783d1c517cac33895c2b81 and its alibaba/zvec submodule cb422972981a2ed4735e9cfb419397c0a2383f02. Submodule license files are fetched at the exact gitlink revisions in that tree, not a similarly named zvec release tag.",
    "The zvec native notices conservatively cover upstream native source dependencies, including optional/test-only declarations where retained. Inclusion of a license text is not proof that every listed component is linked into the binary. The top-level zvec NOTICE additionally covers Unicode 17.0.0 data and pyglass adaptations.",
    "RaBitQ vendored Eigen is MPL-2.0. Supply the exact source subtree include/rabitqlib/third/Eigen from VectorDB-NTU/RaBitQ-Library commit 858b0d6c480766d0e4f08fc5e02f34b53d698fad together with its source notices; a license text alone is insufficient.",
    "For RocksDB dual-licensed components the Apache-2.0 option is selected; preserve LICENSE.leveldb and the range-tree Apache-2.0 license as third-party notices. LZ4 lib/LICENSE is BSD-2-Clause; the optional GPL command-line tools are not part of the intended zvec library payload.",
    "Arrow 21.0.0 declares bundled build dependencies in cpp/thirdparty/versions.txt at ee4d09ebef61c663c1efbfa4c18e518a03b798be; added conservative notices for Boost 1.88.0, RapidJSON 232389d4f1012dddec4ef84861face2d2ba85709, RE2 2022-06-01, Thrift 0.22.0, utf8proc 2.10.0, xsimd 13.0.0 and zlib 1.3.1. Inclusion does not assert every optional dependency is linked in the prebuilt binary.",
    "Eigen 3.4.0 source can be obtained from https://github.com/VectorDB-NTU/RaBitQ-Library/archive/858b0d6c480766d0e4f08fc5e02f34b53d698fad.tar.gz ; the corresponding subtree is include/rabitqlib/third/Eigen. No local modification is made. The checked alibaba/zvec thirdparty/RaBitQ-Library/CMakeLists.txt exposes an include directory and applies no Eigen patch. The generated source-availability text identifies this source and preserves recipients rights.",
    "lxgw-wenkai-webfont 1.7.0 VERSION identifies font v1.250. Restored the complete upstream OFL notice at LXGW tag v1.250, commit f361dc288705e69a9ea292937364130ad77cc932, including Copyright 2021-2023 LXGW and Copyright 2020 The Klee Project Authors; package wrapper MIT remains separate.",
    "RocksDB README.md at 6a436150417120a3f9732d65a2a5c2b8d19b60fc expressly permits choosing Apache-2.0 instead of GPLv2. The PerconaFT range-tree license header is retained verbatim with its copyright notice and Apache-2.0 alternative; the collected GPLv2 text is an upstream alternative, not the selected license."
  ]
